      "bottomRightY": 334,
      "content": "Gamma correction is used to compensate for non-linearity of the display apparatus. This is a non-linear operation that might impact digital image processing. For instance, a threshold is no longer linear. But it can be useful to amplify low-intensity details at the expense of brighter image details.",
